<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kurunta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kurunta was a Hittite prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muwatalli-ii">Muwatalli II</a>, who ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> kingdom of Tarhuntassa in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in the 13th century BCE. His treaty with the great king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tudhaliya-iv">Tudhaliya IV</a>, inscribed on a bronze tablet found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> in 1986, sets out his borders and privileges. Seals from Hattusa suggest that he later claimed the title of great king himself.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kurunta.jpg" alt="Kurunta" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eunostos · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhyton_en_forme_de_cerf_hittite,_exposition_Royaumes_oubli%C3%A9s,_Louvre_2019.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
